{"name":"Immilmar","status":"ok","title":"Immilmar","pageId":14961,"html":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" dir=\"ltr\" lang=\"en\"><p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n</p><aside class=\"portable-infobox pi-background pi-border-color pi-theme-frwiki pi-layout-default type-location\" role=\"region\">\n\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Category:Maps_of_Immilmar\" title=\"Category:Maps of Immilmar\">Gallery</a></nav>\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-item-spacing pi-title pi-secondary-background\" data-source=\"name\">Immilmar</h2>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Geography<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-S.CG-p80_1-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-S.CG-p80-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-UE-p144_2-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-UE-p144-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-UE-p145_3-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-UE-p145-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FRCS-p203_4-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS-p203-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></h2>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"type\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Type</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Settlement</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"region\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Region</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Rashemen\" title=\"Rashemen\">Rashemen</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Unapproachable_East\" title=\"Unapproachable East\">Unapproachable East</a></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"size\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Size</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Large City</div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Society<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-UE-p144_2-1\"><a href=\"#cite_note-UE-p144-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-UE-p145_3-1\"><a href=\"#cite_note-UE-p145-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FRCG-p168_6-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCG-p168-6\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>5<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></h2>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"races\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Races</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><table class=\"percentagetable\"><caption style=\"text-align:center;caption-side:top;\">As of 1372 DR</caption><tbody><tr><td> <a href=\"/wiki/Human\" title=\"Human\">Humans</a> </td><td> 93%  </td></tr><tr><td> <a href=\"/wiki/Spirit_folk\" title=\"Spirit folk\">Spirit folk</a> </td><td> 6%  </td></tr><tr><td> Other  </td><td> 1%  </td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"religion\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Religions</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/The_Three\" title=\"The Three\">The Three</a>: <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/Bhalla\" title=\"Bhalla\">Bhalla</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/Khelliara\" title=\"Khelliara\">Khelliara</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/The_Hidden_One\" title=\"The Hidden One\">The Hidden One</a> (later) <a href=\"/wiki/Sel%C3%BBne\" title=\"Selûne\">Selûne</a><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-5\"><a href=\"#cite_note-5\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>note 1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"alignment\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Alignments</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Neutral_good\" title=\"Neutral good\">Neutral good</a></div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Commerce<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-UE-p145_3-2\"><a href=\"#cite_note-UE-p145-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></h2>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"exports\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Exports</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Iron\" title=\"Iron\">Iron</a> works, leather goods, woodworking</div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Politics</h2>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"rulertype\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Ruler's type</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Iron_Lord\" title=\"Iron Lord\">Iron Lord</a></div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">History<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-UE-p145_3-3\"><a href=\"#cite_note-UE-p145-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FRCG-p168_6-1\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCG-p168-6\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>5<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-DRW-p9_7-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-DRW-p9-7\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>6<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></h2>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"population1\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Population</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">21,210 in <a href=\"/wiki/1372_DR\" title=\"1372 DR\">1372 DR</a><br/>25,000 in <a href=\"/wiki/1479_DR\" title=\"1479 DR\">1479 DR</a></div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"ruler1\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Iron_Lord\" title=\"Iron Lord\">Iron Lord</a></h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><span class=\"new\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvSHlhbW9uX0h1enppdGhsYXI/YWN0aW9uPWVkaXQmcmVkbGluaz0x\" title=\"Hyamon Huzzithlar (page does not exist)\">Hyamon Huzzithlar</span> in <a href=\"/wiki/1357_DR\" title=\"1357 DR\">1357 DR</a><br/><a href=\"/wiki/Volas_Dyervolk\" title=\"Volas Dyervolk\">Volas Dyervolk</a> in <a href=\"/wiki/1372_DR\" title=\"1372 DR\">1372 DR</a><br/><a href=\"/wiki/Mangan_Uruk\" title=\"Mangan Uruk\">Mangan Uruk</a> in <a href=\"/wiki/1479_DR\" title=\"1479 DR\">1479 DR</a></div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Category:Inhabitants_of_Immilmar\" title=\"Category:Inhabitants of Immilmar\">Inhabitants of  Immilmar</a></nav>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Category:Locations_in_Immilmar\" title=\"Category:Locations in Immilmar\">Locations in  Immilmar</a></nav>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Category:Organizations_in_Immilmar\" title=\"Category:Organizations in Immilmar\">Organizations in  Immilmar</a></nav>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><span class=\"DPL-purge plainlinks\"><a class=\"text\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Template:Category_intersection_jump?DPL_cat1=Locations_in__Immilmar&amp;DPL_cat2=Roads&amp;action=purge\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Roads  in  Immilmar</a></span></nav>\n</aside>\n<p class=\"mw-empty-elt\"></p><p><b>Immilmar</b> was the capital city of <a href=\"/wiki/Rashemen\" title=\"Rashemen\">Rashemen</a> and seat of power for the nation's <a href=\"/wiki/Iron_Lord\" title=\"Iron Lord\">Iron Lord</a>.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-S.CG-p80_1-1\"><a href=\"#cite_note-S.CG-p80-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-UE-p144_2-2\"><a href=\"#cite_note-UE-p144-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> Beyond its political importance as the heart of Rashemen, it was perhaps most famous for its great crafters, whose goods were renowned across the <a href=\"/wiki/Unapproachable_East\" title=\"Unapproachable East\">Unapproachable East</a> and the <a href=\"/wiki/Cold_Lands\" title=\"Cold Lands\">Cold Lands</a>.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-UE-p145_3-4\"><a href=\"#cite_note-UE-p145-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<div aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\" class=\"toc\" id=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\"><input class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" role=\"button\" style=\"display:none\" type=\"checkbox\"/><div class=\"toctitle\" dir=\"ltr\" lang=\"en\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Description\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Description</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Geography\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Geography</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Government\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Government</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Trade\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Trade</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Defenses\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Defenses</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#History\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">History</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Notable_Locations\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Notable Locations</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Inhabitants\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Inhabitants</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Notable_Inhabitants\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Notable Inhabitants</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Appendix\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Appendix</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Notes\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Notes</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#References\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">References</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Description\">Description</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Description\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Immilmar?veaction=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Description\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>At the center of Immilmar was the Lord's citadel, built with the help of the mighty <a href=\"/wiki/Wychlaran\" title=\"Wychlaran\">Wychlaran</a>. Around the keep was the central part of Immilmar, that comprised stone buildings that were only found in the country's large cities.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-UE-p144_2-3\"><a href=\"#cite_note-UE-p144-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> While the city's heart bustled with the stone and iron industry for which the city was famous, it was a charming part of the city that was highlighted by footpaths that wound around emerging saplings.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-S.CG-p80_1-2\"><a href=\"#cite_note-S.CG-p80-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-UE-p145_3-5\"><a href=\"#cite_note-UE-p145-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>The homes that were built farther-out were constructed like those found throughout the rest of Rashemen: wood-and-stone lodges that featured steep-sloped roofs.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-S.CG-p80_1-3\"><a href=\"#cite_note-S.CG-p80-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-UE-p144_2-4\"><a href=\"#cite_note-UE-p144-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FRCG-p168_6-2\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCG-p168-6\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>5<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> The waterfront on the western side of the city was a pleasing locale that was always active with fishers and other boat-faring folk.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-S.CG-p81_8-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-S.CG-p81-8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>7<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Geography\">Geography</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Geography\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Immilmar?veaction=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Geography\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The city was set upon the western coast of Rashemen, overlooking the great <a href=\"/wiki/Lake_Ashane\" title=\"Lake Ashane\">Lake Ashane</a>.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-UE-p144_2-5\"><a href=\"#cite_note-UE-p144-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-W.M_9-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-W.M-9\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>8<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Government\">Government</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Government\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Immilmar?veaction=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Government\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>While Immilmar and the entire nation of Rashemen were ruled by the Iron Lord, known by Rashemaar as the Huhrong, the true power was held by the Wychlaran. It was by their permission that the great warrior-rulers were able to wield their power.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-S.CG-p80_1-4\"><a href=\"#cite_note-S.CG-p80-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Trade\">Trade</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Trade\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Immilmar?veaction=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Trade\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Merchants and traders from <a href=\"/wiki/Thesk\" title=\"Thesk\">Thesk</a> and the <a href=\"/wiki/Cold_Lands\" title=\"Cold Lands\">Cold Lands</a> regularly traveled throughout Immilmar, selling wares and goods from their respective homes.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-UE-p144_2-6\"><a href=\"#cite_note-UE-p144-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> Similarly, traders and fisherman from nearby Rashemaar villages come to the city to earn their keep.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-S.CG-p80_1-5\"><a href=\"#cite_note-S.CG-p80-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>Immilmar was renowned for its craftspeople that specialized in working with wood, leather, and <a href=\"/wiki/Iron\" title=\"Iron\">iron</a>.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-UE-p145_3-6\"><a href=\"#cite_note-UE-p145-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Defenses\">Defenses</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Defenses\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Immilmar?veaction=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Defenses\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In addition to the 60 or so berserkers from the local lodges, Immilmar was defended by <i>Iron Lord's Guard</i>, a military group of approximate 1800 warriors.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-UE-p145_3-7\"><a href=\"#cite_note-UE-p145-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"History\">History</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: History\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Immilmar?veaction=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: History\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Originally a fortress of the ancient <a href=\"/wiki/Narfell\" title=\"Narfell\">Narfell</a> Empire, <a href=\"/wiki/Huhrong%27s_Citadel\" title=\"Huhrong's Citadel\">Huhrong's Citadel</a> was built around the ruins, and the rest of the city were built out from there.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-SB.CG-p80_10-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-SB.CG-p80-10\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>9<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>The city was partially flood in the <a href=\"/wiki/1365_DR\" title=\"1365 DR\">Year of the Sword, 1365 DR</a>, when agents of <a href=\"/wiki/Thay\" title=\"Thay\">Thay</a> melted a portion of the glacier that covered the <a href=\"/wiki/Icerim_Mountains\" title=\"Icerim Mountains\">Icerim Mountains</a>.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-UE-p141_11-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-UE-p141-11\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>10<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-GHotR-p147_12-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-GHotR-p147-12\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>11<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>Some <a href=\"/wiki/1368_DR\" title=\"1368 DR\">years later</a> gangs of murderers somehow <i><a href=\"/wiki/Teleport\" title=\"Teleport\">teleported</a></i> into Immilmar and began slaying important city leaders. They were defeated in short order by the resident <a href=\"/wiki/Rashemaar_berserkers\" title=\"Rashemaar berserkers\">berserkers</a>.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-UE-p141_11-1\"><a href=\"#cite_note-UE-p141-11\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>10<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-GHotR-p149_13-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-GHotR-p149-13\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>12<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Notable_Locations\">Notable Locations</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Notable Locations\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Immilmar?veaction=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Notable Locations\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<dl><dt>Businesses</dt>\n<dd></dd></dl>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/Carvers%27_Hall\" title=\"Carvers' Hall\">Carvers' Hall</a>, the guildhouse of the city's skilled artisans.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-S.CG-p82_14-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-S.CG-p82-14\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>13<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Blackstone_House\" title=\"Blackstone House\">Blackstone House</a>, the finest inn of the city that catered to foreign traders.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-UE-p145_3-8\"><a href=\"#cite_note-UE-p145-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-S.CG-p82_14-1\"><a href=\"#cite_note-S.CG-p82-14\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>13<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/The_Guardian_Witch\" title=\"The Guardian Witch\">The Guardian Witch</a>, a cozy inn that catered to local fishers.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-S.CG-p81_8-1\"><a href=\"#cite_note-S.CG-p81-8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>7<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li></ul>\n<dl><dt>Landmarks</dt>\n<dd></dd></dl>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/Immilmar/City_Market\" title=\"Immilmar/City Market\">City Market</a>, the bustling covered market in which anyone could buy local goods or products imported from outlanders.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-S.CG-p81_8-2\"><a href=\"#cite_note-S.CG-p81-8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>7<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li>Communal longhouse, a feasting all and venue for the meetings of the local elders.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-S.CG-p81_8-3\"><a href=\"#cite_note-S.CG-p81-8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>7<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Huhrong%27s_Citadel\" title=\"Huhrong's Citadel\">Huhrong's Citadel</a>, the great stone fortress of the Iron Lord and home to his family.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-UE-p144_2-7\"><a href=\"#cite_note-UE-p144-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-S.CG-p82_14-2\"><a href=\"#cite_note-S.CG-p82-14\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>13<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li>Smith's Quarter, an area of Immilmar highlighted by the numerous smithies, including that of <a href=\"/wiki/Tholli_Ironweaver\" title=\"Tholli Ironweaver\">Tholli Ironweaver</a>.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-UE-p145_3-9\"><a href=\"#cite_note-UE-p145-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Witches%27_Hall\" title=\"Witches' Hall\">Witches' Hall</a>, the sacred meeting place of the city's <a href=\"/wiki/Hathran\" title=\"Hathran\">hathrans</a>.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-UE-p145_3-10\"><a href=\"#cite_note-UE-p145-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-S.CG-p83_15-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-S.CG-p83-15\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>14<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li></ul>\n<dl><dt>Temples</dt>\n<dd></dd></dl>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/House_of_Bhalla\" title=\"House of Bhalla\">House of Bhalla</a>, a holy house of <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/Bhalla\" title=\"Bhalla\">Bhalla</a> that ensured that the worship of the goddess did not stray too far from official doctrine.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-UE-p144_2-8\"><a href=\"#cite_note-UE-p144-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-UE-p145_3-11\"><a href=\"#cite_note-UE-p145-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Inhabitants\">Inhabitants</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Inhabitants\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Immilmar?veaction=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Inhabitants\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Along with the great trading city of <a href=\"/wiki/Mulptan\" title=\"Mulptan\">Mulptan</a>, Immilmar was one locale in Rashemen where outlanders were welcome. Rashemaar leaders even allowed councilors from nearby nations such as <a href=\"/wiki/Aglarond\" title=\"Aglarond\">Aglarond</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Damara\" title=\"Damara\">Damara</a>, and <a href=\"/wiki/Impiltur\" title=\"Impiltur\">Impiltur</a> to take up residence within their nations' embassies.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-UE-p144_2-9\"><a href=\"#cite_note-UE-p144-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FRCG-p168_6-3\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCG-p168-6\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>5<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>Immilmar housed a number of lodge-houses of the <a href=\"/wiki/Rashemaar_berserkers\" title=\"Rashemaar berserkers\">Rashemaar berserkers</a>, including those of the <a href=\"/wiki/Goblin_lodge\" title=\"Goblin lodge\">Goblin</a>,<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-S.CG-p83_15-1\"><a href=\"#cite_note-S.CG-p83-15\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>14<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> <a href=\"/wiki/Great_Stag_lodge\" title=\"Great Stag lodge\">Great Stag</a>, and <a href=\"/wiki/Owlbear_lodge\" title=\"Owlbear lodge\">Owlbear lodges</a>.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-UE-p145_3-12\"><a href=\"#cite_note-UE-p145-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-S.CG-p81_8-4\"><a href=\"#cite_note-S.CG-p81-8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>7<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Notable_Inhabitants\">Notable Inhabitants</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Notable Inhabitants\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Immilmar?veaction=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Notable Inhabitants\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/Othlor\" title=\"Othlor\">Othlor</a> <a href=\"/wiki/Fydra_Night-Tree\" title=\"Fydra Night-Tree\">Fydra Night-Tree</a>, leader of  the city's Wychlaran and advisor to the Iron Lord.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-UE-p145_3-13\"><a href=\"#cite_note-UE-p145-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><span class=\"new\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvUmluZGFsYV9TaGFyZHJvb24/YWN0aW9uPWVkaXQmcmVkbGluaz0x\" title=\"Rindala Shardroon (page does not exist)\">Rindala Shardroon</span>, the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/Sage\" title=\"Sage\">sage</a> of Immilmar.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-D272-96_16-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-D272-96-16\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>15<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Appendix\">Appendix</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Appendix\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Immilmar?veaction=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Appendix\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Notes\">Notes</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Notes\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Immilmar?veaction=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Notes\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<small><div class=\"mw-references-wrap\"><ol class=\"references\">\n<li id=\"cite_note-5\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-5\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\">Following the events of the <a href=\"/wiki/Spellplague\" title=\"Spellplague\">Spellplague</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Sel%C3%BBne\" title=\"Selûne\">Selûne</a> was worshipped as a member of <a href=\"/wiki/The_Three\" title=\"The Three\">The Three</a> as <a href=\"/wiki/Mystra\" title=\"Mystra\">Mystra</a> was absent from the <a href=\"/wiki/Faer%C3%BBnian_pantheon\" title=\"Faerûnian pantheon\">Faerûnian pantheon</a>.</span>\n</li>\n</ol></div></small>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"References\">References</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: References\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Immilmar?veaction=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: References\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<div class=\"reflist\" style=\"\">\n<div class=\"mw-references-wrap mw-references-columns\"><ol class=\"references\">\n<li id=\"cite_note-S.CG-p80-1\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\">↑ <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-S.CG-p80_1-0\">1.0</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-S.CG-p80_1-1\">1.1</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-S.CG-p80_1-2\">1.2</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-S.CG-p80_1-3\">1.3</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-S.CG-p80_1-4\">1.4</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-S.CG-p80_1-5\">1.5</a></sup></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a href=\"/wiki/Anthony_Pryor\" title=\"Anthony Pryor\">Anthony Pryor</a> (June 1995). “Campaign Guide”. In <a href=\"/wiki/Michele_Carter\" title=\"Michele Carter\">Michele Carter</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Doug_Stewart\" title=\"Doug Stewart\">Doug Stewart</a> eds. <i><a href=\"/wiki/Spellbound\" title=\"Spellbound\">Spellbound</a></i> (<a href=\"/wiki/TSR,_Inc.\" title=\"TSR, Inc.\">TSR, Inc.</a>), p. 80. ISBN <a href=\"/wiki/Special:BookSources/978-0786901395\" title=\"Special:BookSources/978-0786901395\">978-0786901395</a>.</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-UE-p144-2\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\">↑ <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-UE-p144_2-0\">2.00</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-UE-p144_2-1\">2.01</a></sup> <s